package api

import (
	"net/http"
)

var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodPatch,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/issues/{key}/nodes/{id}",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: "Move the node {id} names {parent?, after?, actor?}: under the node parent names, among its siblings where after names one, in one write. {id} is the node's store address under the issue, percent-encoded as one path segment, read as the state route reads it; a node the caller may not see under the issue is 404 NOT_FOUND, and so is a parent the caller may not see. The request names the placement it read in If-Match: the node's placement_seq, the seq of its current part_of, which the tree read answers on every node, as a quoted entity tag; a move with no If-Match is 428 PRECONDITION_REQUIRED, and one whose tag is no longer the node's placement_seq 412 PRECONDITION_FAILED, so a move taken against a parent that has since changed stores nothing. A body with neither parent nor after is 400 MOVE_INPUT. A parent appends one part_of tuple from the node to the new parent and one retraction of the old, at no event, and touches no descendant and no serves; a ranked node takes a rank of its own document's band between after and the next ranked sibling of that band, after null placing it first in its band (after the issue's memo, for a block of the spec's band under the issue) and no after after every ranked sibling of its band; an after that is no ranked child of the parent, the node itself, or of another band, and an after on a node that holds no rank, are 400 INVALID_POINTER naming after. A block of a document holds the placement stored, which every later index pass keeps but where an edit names another parent in a typed block's parent attribute, takes the block's parent out of the text, or gives a decision a from_ask naming an ask of its issue, under which it then stands. Where Markdown can show the block's new place - under its document's top level, a callout or a list item that stands in no decision, reading, ask, requirement, criterion, check or plan_task - its text moves there in the same transaction, under the room's lock, and a typed block's parent attribute names the new parent, or is taken out where it can name none (a lens, a finding, a risk, a constraint, a result, an issue or a document); a move that names no parent keeps that attribute as it stands; a change of the text writes one version of the document, with its artifact.version, which moves the document's open approval request; a text move that would leave a callout or a list item with no block of its own - its last block, or a list item's own first paragraph - is 409 CONTAINER_WOULD_EMPTY, naming the container and its kind. Where the move changes a query of a converted issue, the issue's queries are marked owed in the write and their versions written once it has committed. Refusals, in order: an ask, a comment or a message is 400 NODE_NOT_MOVABLE, naming it and its kind, and so is a decision that holds a from_ask, which stands under the ask it settles, naming the decision, and that ask where the caller may read it; a constraint under any node but an issue's is 400 INVALID_POINTER; a body with neither parent nor after is 400 MOVE_INPUT, and a move with no If-Match 428 PRECONDITION_REQUIRED; then, under the owner locks of the issue and of every issue a node of the node's subtree or the parent's chain stands under, on an issue Legion runs, a move of a requirement, criterion or check by a session that is no person and no architect of the issue or of an issue above it is 403 DOCUMENT_WRITER_NOT_ARCHITECT; a caller who holds no person scope moving a person's decision - an answered ask, the :::ask block of one, or a decision a person decided - is 409 ANSWERED_ASK_KEPT, quoting it; a tag that is no longer the node's placement_seq is 412 PRECONDITION_FAILED; a node under an issue the move did not lock at each of two attempts is 409 PARENT_CONTENDED; a parent inside the node's subtree, one outside the issue's own tree, and a node that reads its issue from its own row under a node of an issue below are 400 INVALID_POINTER; a parent that is, or stands under, the node of a document a removal could take, where only a lens, a finding or a risk stands, is 409 PARENT_DOCUMENT_REMOVABLE, naming the node and its kind, the parent and the document; a parent the walk of its issue does not reach - gone, a comment or a message the conversation test does not pass, or under one - is 409 PARENT_NOT_REACHED, naming the parent and why; an after that is no ranked sibling of the node's band is 400 INVALID_POINTER, naming after; and last, under the room locks, a text move that would leave a callout or a list item with no block of its own is 409 CONTAINER_WOULD_EMPTY, naming the container and its kind. A refused move stores nothing. Answers 200 {parent, after, placement_seq}: the parent's store address, the ranked sibling the node now follows or null, and the new placement_seq, the tag the next If-Match of the node takes.",
	Handler:     (*server).moveNodeRoute,
	WriteClass:  scopeProject,
	ID:          &idRoute{Reason: "a node's store address under the issue, which FindNodeUnderIssue decodes and no prefix shortens"},
	// The move of a node (node_move.go): its parent and its place among its siblings, answered with
	// the parent, the sibling it follows and the new placement_seq.
	Shape: routeShape{
		Status: http.StatusOK, Response: nodeMoved{}, Request: nodeMoveInput{},
		Headers: []routeHeader{placementIfMatch},
	},
})
